Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Samara-Weaving.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **Azrael (2024) is missing entirely.** She led a dialogue-free horror film — no spoken English for the runtime, entirely physical performance. This is the best available refutation of the "one register, single sustained scream" charge the draft raises in section 6 and then answers only with a trust argument. It's also the literal payoff of the childhood thread the draft builds and never collects on: the kid who went silent for weeks at every new school headlines a movie where speaking gets you killed. Strongest candidate for a new section.

2. **No Emma Frost / X-Men casting**, and it's the fact that pressure-tests the thesis. Section 6 argues she returns to small rooms because trust is expensive and slow to earn — then she signs onto the most opaque machine in the industry, where that audit can't be run and the fame she says she never wanted isn't optional. The draft should hold that tension rather than leave the trust-inventory explanation unchallenged.

Also flagged: the first child (born late May 2026) and *Carolina Caroline* are both claimed as current-tense anchors in the formula-fingerprint ledger but appear nowhere in the body — and the Rabbit Hole references the airport/Margot Robbie story before the closing section tells it, spoiling the best ending in recent people drafts.

Sources: [Azrael review — Bloody Disgusting](https://bloody-disgusting.com/reviews/3832663/azrael-review-samara-weaving-stuns-in-dialogue-free-biblical-survival-horror-movie/), [Emma Frost casting — Variety](https://variety.com/2026/film/news/x-men-movie-cast-samara-weaving-emma-frost-1236825209/), [First child — extratv](https://extratv.com/2026/05/27/ready-or-not-2-star-samara-weaving-welcomes-first-child/)
